WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.950
Marvel Comics' Eternals are an ancient, cosmic
race who live on Saturn's moon Titan.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.650
If Marvel Studios embraces all the cosmos-spanning
wonder of the group's comic-book appearances

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.520
in the upcoming Eternals movie, viewers have
some technicolor treats in store.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.320
Here's the lowdown on the Eternals.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.240
The Eternals were created by comics legend
Jack Kirby in 1976.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.500
They're an ancient race of superbeings who
have long protected Earth from evil, specifically

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.410
the rule of the treacherous Deviants.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.130
The original Eternals series tells a meticulously
plotted tale and was created with an ending

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:31.620
in mind.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.480
Unfortunately, Kirby never reached his intended
finale.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.360
The Eternals was axed at issue #19 before
Kirby had a chance to wrap up all of the existing

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.140
plot threads.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.460
It lingered unfinished for a while until writers
Roy Thomas and Mark Gruenwald used a storyline

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.140
that ended with Thor #301 to wrap up the tale
of the Eternals' cosmic crusade.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.730
We're glad the story ended up resolved, but
we'll always be wondering what it could have

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.740
looked like if Kirby had a chance to finish
the series as he intended.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.910
While their name was on the cover, the Eternals
arguably weren't the breakout stars of their

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:02.400
own book.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.840
That was the Celestials, the "Space Gods"
that created the Eternals, the Deviants, and,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.140
it turns out, pretty much all sentient life
in the Marvel Universe.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:14.580
The Celestials were an example of Kirby building
on an idea he'd explored in other comics.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:19.080
They were a step past Galactus, who he and
Stan Lee had created in Fantastic Four: a

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.090
massive humanoid that was essentially a living
force of nature with ties to the origins of

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:23.780
the universe.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.680
Even their designs were similar, clad in Kirby's
trademark elaborate armor, but while Galactus

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.270
had a recognizable human face, the Celestials
were completely covered by their armor, making

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.680
them far more unknowable.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.550
The Celestials were defined by the ongoing
life creation experiment that they'd been

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.200
tinkering with for billions of years, with
names that indicated their function.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.380
Gammemnon the Gatherer, for example, was charged
with acquiring samples of life from across

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.100
the universe.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.420
Arishem the Judge would determine whether
a planet's population would live or die once

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.300
the experiment had run its course, and Exitar
the Exterminator, well, you can guess his

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:55.800
job.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.920
While characters like Ikaris have often been
overlooked, the Celestials were woven into

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.040
the fabric of the Marvel Universe, with connections
to everything from the X-Men to the Infinity

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:04.540
Stones.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.700
The Avengers have even set up a headquarters
in a building made from the body of a long-dead

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.200
Celestial.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.740
You can't create a team of superheroes without
giving them proper antagonists.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.830
There must always be a Loki for every Thor,
and Kirby knew this good and well when approaching

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.240
the Eternals, so he gave them the Deviants.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.640
When the Celestials created the Eternals,
they also created the Deviants, a horrifying

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.630
race of creatures that are, physically, the
opposite of the beautiful humanoid Eternals.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:32.660
The two species are caught in a constant war
between one another, with the Deviants forming

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.280
a sort of natural opposition.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:39.180
No Deviant mutation is repeated in their species,
so each physical anomaly or superpower is

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.060
unique to the Deviant who possesses it.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.600
They are, effectively, mutations of the Eternals.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.200
Thousands of years ago, the Deviants resided
on Earth and conquered much of early humanity.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.240
The Eternals ended their reign, though Deviants
still live on Earth to this day and clash

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.720
with Eternals regularly.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.300
Kirby's stories were often more inspired by
timeless literary classics than they were

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.220
by other comics.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.540
His Thor stories are very much Shakespearean,
while the Fantastic Four draws heavily from

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.430
sci-fi literature and classic monster movies.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.540
It only makes sense that he'd carry that ethos
into creating the Eternals.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.280
Kirby is on the record as naming two novels
as primary influences on the series.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.400
The first is sci-fi master Arthur C. Clarke's
Childhood's End.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.000
This novel in particular influenced Kirby's
interpretation of the Celestials as well as

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.510
the Uni-Mind, a massively powerful composite
of several Eternals.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.319
He also drew heavily from Erich von Daniken's
Chariot of the Gods, a nonfiction book that

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.040
posits the idea of alien gods.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.000
It's proof that the best way to tell great
stories is to draw inspiration from a wealth

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.360
of sources, not just from the medium or genre
in which you work.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.160
It makes sense that the filmmakers behind
the MCU would bring the Eternals into play.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.180
They already have a tie to the world at this
point.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.460
Eternals such as Starfox, Sersi, and Makkari
can already be easily introduced to the world

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.880
through their family's presence in the MCU
in the form of the Mad Titan himself, Thanos.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.760
"I am...inevitable."

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.860
Thanos is perhaps the most famous of the Eternals.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.280
While he wasn't introduced in the original
Kirby series, Jim Starlin, the creator of

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.380
Thanos, designed him as an extension of their
world.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.120
Thanos is a Deviant child of an Eternal mother
and father, a being born into a world that

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.450
instantly rejected him.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.729
His mother was so disgusted with him from
birth that she tried to kill him as a child.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:22.689
His traumatic childhood only furthered his
fascination with Death, which eventually led

00:04:22.689 --> 00:04:24.099
to him becoming the Mad Titan.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.440
While he's very rarely associated with the
Eternals directly these days, he's very much

00:04:28.449 --> 00:04:29.789
a product of their society.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:34.900
The Eternals' relationship with their creators,
the Celestials, is a bit turbulent.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.969
They've at times found themselves on opposing
sides of the battlefield.

00:04:37.969 --> 00:04:42.540
The Celestials, being giant omnipotent immortal
beings, are pretty hard to take on in battle,

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.240
so it makes sense that, on what may be the
most famous occasion during which the two

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.559
races came to blows, the Eternals didn't go
at it alone.

00:04:49.559 --> 00:04:52.449
Who better to take on the Celestials than
another race of gods?

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:56.449
The Eternals offered their aid to the forces
of Asgard when the two sides found themselves

00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:57.440
at odds with the Celestials.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.680
The Eternals formed the Uni-Mind, which is
kind of like an Eternal Megazord, while Odin

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.220
possessed the Destroyer armor and enlarged
it to be the size of the Celestials.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.419
Kind of like Ultraman.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.720
It might not get the recognition the Avengers
and X-Men do whenever they join forces, but

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:13.600
we think it's one of the cooler moments in
the history of the Eternals.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.009
A bunch of giant mega-powerful space gods
and robots duking it out is a pretty solid

00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:19.509
story as far as we're concerned.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:24.249
Thanos and his brother Starfox are just about
as polar opposite as they could be.

00:05:24.249 --> 00:05:26.560
Thanos is a massive, purple death-worshipping
supervillain.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.780
Starfox, on the other hand, is a conventionally
attractive ladies' man who typically fights

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:31.660
on the side of good.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.389
His hair is always perfect.

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:36.200
That being said, Starfox is far from squeaky
clean.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:40.919
His rather appropriate real name is Eros,
the same name as the Greek god of love, and

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:45.830
his superpower allows him to manipulate emotions,
especially romantic ones, which has occasionally

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.169
gotten him into legal trouble.

00:05:47.169 --> 00:05:51.509
He's specifically put on trial for harassment
after a married woman claims he used his powers

00:05:51.509 --> 00:05:52.420
to seduce her.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.480
His lawyer in the case is none other than
Jennifer Walters, better known as She-Hulk.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.800
It's a story that could be taken as a one-note
joke, but instead becomes a genuinely compelling

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.880
look into the ethics of Starfox's powers.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.909
It comes to light that he's used them to not
only make people attracted to him but to influence

00:06:06.909 --> 00:06:07.940
the feelings of others.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.860
He's responsible for Walters' marriage to
John Jameson and is briefly convinced that

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.400
he triggered Thanos' initial infatuation with
Death.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.449
The story ends with Starfox agreeing to have
his powers shut down so that he won't be able

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:19.780
to hurt anyone else with them.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.260
There's something about super-speed that just
feels right.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.619
It's not too complicated.

00:06:24.619 --> 00:06:26.589
It doesn't make the user omnipotently powerful.

00:06:26.589 --> 00:06:28.830
It's perhaps the most perfect superpower.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:32.580
As such, it makes sense that there are so
many comic-book superheroes and villains that

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.460
run really fast.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:38.100
Marvel alone has Quicksilver, Whizzer, and
among others, Makkari, a member of the Eternals

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:38.600
family.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.400
But even he's not the fastest out there.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.360
An issue of Quasar written by Mark Gruenwald
features a grand race between all of the speedsters

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.640
in the Marvel universe, including Makkari.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.000
The one that comes out on top, however, isn't
a character we've seen before.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.120
He's an amnesiac from a different universe.

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:56.760
Even he doesn't remember his real name, though
he seems to recall it being something like

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.520
"Buried Alien."

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.800
This issue came out just after DC Comics'
the Flash, also known as Barry Allen, had

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.800
perished in Crisis on Infinite Earths.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.700
Gruenwald very clearly included Buried Alien
as an homage to the character.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.560
The Eternals generally keep to themselves.

00:07:10.749 --> 00:07:14.080
Their stories are often pretty contained and
don't bleed out into the rest of the Marvel

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:14.660
universe.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.960
But there are exceptions to every rule, and
the Eternal known as Sersi is one of them.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.020
Sersi is pretty largely integrated into the
world of Marvel.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.759
She can cast illusions, has super strength,
and has the ability to teleport.

00:07:25.759 --> 00:07:28.969
Sersi was, for a time, even a member of the
Avengers.

00:07:28.969 --> 00:07:31.509
She joined at the invitation of none other
than Captain America.

00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:35.439
Her decision to join the team at the time
is just as much motivated by her desire to

00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:39.849
do good as it is by her infatuation with the
Star-Spangled Avenger, which she's harbored

00:07:39.849 --> 00:07:40.700
for quite some time.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.860
Her tenure on the team came to a close in
the 1990s.

00:07:44.009 --> 00:07:47.979
She has since aided the team on occasion,
and while she's yet to properly woo Cap, we're

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.320
sure she's not done trying.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.820
Ultron has been a thorn in the side of the
heroes of the Marvel universe for decades.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:58.270
Fueled by an abject hatred of humanity, the
evil robot's sole mission is the extermination

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.060
of humanity.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.900
So what happens when Ultron is introduced
to the power of love?

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:06.619
In the graphic novel Rage of Ultron, we see
what happens when Starfox's emotion manipulation

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:08.169
powers meet the robot menace.

00:08:08.169 --> 00:08:12.949
In the story's finale, Ultron and his creator,
Hank Pym, have merged into a singular being

00:08:12.949 --> 00:08:15.320
prepared to wipe out humanity once and for
all.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:19.800
Starfox is able to defeat them by using his
powers to introduce love into the equation.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:24.029
The encounter takes Ultron and Hank back to
the moment the robot was activated and makes

00:08:24.029 --> 00:08:28.320
both of them re-evaluate it, recognizing their
love for each other as a sort of father and

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:28.820
son.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.040
"I wanted to show you.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.600
I don't have anyone else."

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.820
Ultron's introduction to love is enough to
get him to back off and banish himself into

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:38.960
the depths of space.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.020
Starfox's powers may make him a weird creep
sometimes, but they've also managed to save

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.160
the world at least once.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.680
When it was announced in April 2018, Eternals
one of the more surprising entries in Phase

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:53.140
4 of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, but there
was a hint of what was to come all the way

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:57.220
back in 2014, with a brief cameo in another
surprising Marvel movie.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.080
In Guardians of the Galaxy, when the Collector
is explaining the Infinity Stones, we get

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:05.320
an unmistakable glimpse of a Celestial using
the Power Stone to eradicate the population

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.520
of some unfortunate planet.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:11.020
Knowhere is the severed head of a Celestial,
and Ego identifies himself as a Celestial

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.470
in Guardians Vol. 2.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.360
"I'm what's called a Celestial, sweetheart."

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.100
"A Celestial, like, a god?"

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.160
"Small 'g,' son."

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:25.560
Five years after that first glimpse of the
eons-long saga of Eternals, Deviants, and

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.990
Celestials, we finally got a better idea of
what we can expect when Eternals hits the

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:30.330
screen in 2020.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:34.160
At Marvel's panel at San Diego Comic-Con,
fans were introduced to the main cast.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.280
"Everybody, big round of applause to the Eternals!"

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:43.660
Interestingly enough, while the movie was
originally billed as focusing on Ikaris and

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.380
Sersi, the latter character was absent from
the announcement.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:50.500
Instead, we were introduced to Richard Madden,
best known as Robb Stark from Game of Thrones,

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:55.690
as Ikaris, Angelina Jolie as Thena, Salma
Hayek as Ajak, stand-up comedian and Academy

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:00.830
Award-nominated screenwriter Kumail Nanjiani
as Kingo, former Miss Deaf America and Walking

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:06.610
Dead actress Lauren Ridloff as Makkari, Atlanta's
Brian Tyree Henry as Phastos, Korean megastar

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:09.440
Don Lee as Gilgamesh and Lia McHugh as Sprite.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.700
As for the plot, no details have been released
just yet, but if the Celestials are out there

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.820
obliterating planets, someone should probably
deal with that.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.100
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:22.500
Plus, even more Looper videos about Marvel
superheroes are coming soon.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.660
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

